Design a module that drives a 7-segment display based on a 4-bit input value representing a Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD). When the `select` signal is high, the module outputs the corresponding 7-segment encoding for values 0-9, as well as specific patterns for values 10-15, enabling visualization of the BCD input. If `select` is low, all segments are turned off. This module effectively functions as a decoder for displaying BCD values or a fixed pattern on a 7-segment display.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] IN,
    input select,
    output reg [6:0] OUT
);

