description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input into its corresponding 4-bit Gray code output. The circuit uses bitwise XOR operations to ensure that only one bit changes between consecutive values, which is the defining characteristic of Gray code. The first bit of the Gray code output is derived directly from the most significant bit of the binary input, while the remaining bits are calculated based on XORing pairs of adjacent bits from the binary input. The design inherently allows for reset functionality, although the reset signal is not explicitly implemented in this section of the code.
module top_module(
    input  rst,
    input  [3:0] bin_in,
    output [3:0] gray_out
);

